f("p1-head",P1,r"^Closing Disclosure$",("rows",36,576,2),"Closing Disclosure (form H-25)","Issued 4/15/2013","The final, five-page statement of the loan's terms and every closing cost. It replaces the HUD-1 and the final Truth-in-Lending statement for most mortgages (TRID, Reg Z §1026.38).","The borrower must RECEIVE it at least 3 business days before consummation (signing). Received by mail is presumed 3 business days after mailing. A new 3-day wait is required only if the APR becomes inaccurate, the loan product changes, or a prepayment penalty is added (§1026.19(f)).","\"This is your final loan paperwork. It shows the same things your Loan Estimate did, but with the real numbers. We'll compare the two side by side, page by page, before you sign anything.\"","Put the last Loan Estimate next to it. Same loan type, product, rate and amount? If the APR rose more than 1/8% (fixed) the 3-day clock restarts.","overview")
f("p1-issued",P1,r"^Date Issued",("row",36,225),"Date Issued","4/15/2013","The date the creditor (or settlement agent) issued this version of the CD.","Start the 3-business-day count from receipt, not issue, unless delivered in person or e-signed. Business day here = every day except Sundays and federal holidays.","\"This is the date your final numbers were sent. The law gives you three business days to review them before signing.\"","Is the closing date at least 3 business days after you RECEIVED it? (Sample shows the same day — that's only because it's an illustration.)","header")
f("p1-closing",P1,r"^Closing Date",("row",36,225),"Closing Date","4/15/2013","The date the borrower signs (consummation). In California escrow states this is usually signing day, which can differ from funding/recording.","Consummation date drives the 3-day CD receipt rule.","\"This is the day you sign the loan documents. Your three-day review period counts back from here.\"","Matches the escrow instructions and the lock expiration?","header")
f("p1-disb",P1,r"^Disbursement Date",("row",36,225),"Disbursement Date","4/15/2013","The date the lender's money is paid out — when prepaid interest starts.","Prepaid interest (Section F) is calculated from this date to the end of the month (or the day before the first payment period).","\"This is when the loan funds. Interest starts on this day, which is why you'll see a few days of interest in Section F.\"","In CA, if funding/recording slips a day, prepaid interest changes — expect a small difference at the final CD.","header")
f("p1-agent",P1,r"^Settlement Agent",("rows",36,225,2),"Settlement Agent & File #","Epsilon Title Co. · 12-3456","The company running the closing (escrow/title) and its file number.","In California this is the escrow company; title may be the same or a different company.","\"This is the escrow company handling your closing. If anyone calls about wiring money, verify the instructions by calling this company at a number you already know.\"","Wire-fraud check: never wire using instructions sent by email alone.","header")
