f("p1-ppp",P1,r"^Prepayment Penalty",("rows",36,576,2),"Prepayment Penalty","YES — as high as $3,240 in the first 2 years","Whether paying the loan off early (sale or refinance) triggers a penalty.","Only allowed on certain fixed-rate qualified mortgages that are not higher-priced: max 2% of the balance in years 1–2, 1% in year 3, none after; the lender must also offer an alternative without one (§1026.43(g)). Adding one after the last CD restarts the 3-day wait. Most loans today have NONE.","\"This sample loan has a penalty of up to $3,240 if you pay it off within 2 years. Yours says NO — you can pay it off or refinance any time without a penalty.\"","Ours should read NO. If YES, stop and review — it should never be a surprise.","terms")
