f("p1-pp",P1,r"^Projected Payments$",("to",36,576,r"^Estimated Taxes, Insurance"),"Projected Payments","Years 1–7: $1,050.26 · Years 8–30: $967.91","How the total payment changes over time — up to 4 columns (changes in MI, rate, interest-only periods).","Mortgage insurance falls off in year 8 here because borrower-paid PMI terminates automatically when the loan reaches 78% of the original value on the original schedule (Homeowners Protection Act). FHA MIP can be for life.","\"Your payment starts at $1,050.26 — principal and interest $761.78, mortgage insurance $82.35 and escrow $206.13. Around year 8 the mortgage insurance drops off, so it goes to about $967.91. Escrow can change each year with taxes and insurance.\"","$761.78 + $82.35 + $206.13 = $1,050.26. Escrow matches page 4.","payments")
f("p1-mi",P1,r"^Mortgage Insurance$",("row",36,576),"Mortgage Insurance (monthly)","$82.35 years 1–7, then —","The monthly MI premium (conventional PMI, FHA annual MIP or USDA annual fee).","Conventional PMI: can request removal at 80% LTV, automatic at 78% of the original value. FHA: 11 years if 10%+ down, otherwise life of loan.","\"Because you put less than 20% down, there's $82.35 a month of mortgage insurance. It protects the lender, not you, and it comes off automatically once you've paid down to 78% of the original value — or you can ask to remove it at 80%.\"","Matches the MI quote / LE. Removal plan explained.","payments")
